      "side": 0,
      "message": "The Zephyr functions `gpio_pin_get_dt()` and `gpio_pin_get()` return the logical level of the pin.  These routine return 1 if the state of the pin is active.\n\nJason has added the `GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW` flag to this pin:\n```\ngpio_usb_c0_tcpc_int_odl: usb_c0_tcpc_int_odl {\n\tgpios \u003d \u003c\u0026gpio7 3 (GPIO_INPUT | GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW)\u003e;\n\tenum-name \u003d \"GPIO_USB_C0_TCPC_INT_ODL\";\n};\n```\n\nSo `gpio_pin_get_dt()` returns 1 when the interrupt is asserted to the physical/raw state of 0.",
